id: pm-sx52hr
title: "Built-in help examples teach an explicit --author on dozens of commands, training every agent to suppress its own detected identity and pay tokens for it"
description: "src/cli/help-content.ts publishes --author \"codex-agent\" or --assignee codex-agent in the canonical examples for claim, release, close, delete, restore, comments, history-compact, activity, create, list, next, calendar, ctx and more, and src/cli/register-operations.ts repeats it for claim and start-task. An agent reading help learns that passing an author is normal pm usage. Two costs follow. First, correctness: an explicit --author outranks detection, so following the published example replaces real harness and model provenance with a literal string and mislabels author_source as asserted. Second, tokens: the identity fragment is pure overhead repeated in every example an agent reads and in every command it then copies, which is the same budget the token-efficiency work is trying to shrink. The examples predate harness detection and were never revised when pm-z9x1r2 shipped. Every example should show the short form, and the one example that legitimately demonstrates an override should say why an override is the exception."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[7]: agent-ux,"area:cli",author,defect,docs,identity,token-efficiency
created_at: "2026-07-25T12:26:08.788Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-26T17:25:58.316Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-25T20:06:53.511Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: "No published example passes --author or --assignee except the one example whose subject is identity override itself, and that example states why an override is the exception; A contract test asserts the identity-flag fragment appears in at most that one example across help content, operation registrations, docs, and scaffolds; Published examples are asserted to be the shortest form that still demonstrates the command's subject, with a measured token delta recorded as evidence on this item; The identity-override example is cross-referenced to the detection contract so the exception stays discoverable"
goal: project management = context management
objective: The published example for every command is the shortest correct form of that command
value: "Help text is the highest-leverage instruction surface pm has: an agent copies it far more often than it reads prose docs, so a wrong example is a defect multiplied by every agent that reads it"
impact: "Shortens dozens of published examples, restores detected identity for agents that copy them, and removes repeated per-example token overhead"
outcome: "An agent that copies pm help verbatim produces minimal, correctly attributed commands"
parent: pm-mpbb
risk: low
confidence: 85
release: v2026.7.26
resolution: Removed redundant author/assignee tokens from normal agent help while preserving one intentional service-account override example.
expected_result: Agent-facing help is materially more token-efficient without hiding explicit override semantics.
actual_result: "Surface reduced from approximately 141 to 17 tokens across measured examples; help, contracts, and token-budget gates pass."
